\paragraph{Practitioner guidelines.}
When RLVR recovery is planned, prefer CKA-only or high-$\alpha$ \rasp{} ($\alpha \geq 2.0$); the inverted-U (Figure~\ref{fig:dose_response}) shows moderate diversity weighting outperforms both extremes.
When only SFT is available, the criterion still matters (CKA-only exceeds Standard by 4.62\,pp at 20\%) but the margin is smaller than the reward gap suggests.  Maintain per-layer floors ($\geq$40\% retention), stay below 25\% sparsity (\S\ref{sec:sparsity_cliff}), and monitor early-step $f_0$ as a cheap pruning quality diagnostic.

\paragraph{Scope and outlook.}
Reward-accuracy decoupling holds across all tested sparsity levels ($|\Delta| \leq 1$\,pp at 15--25\%); cross-scale (1.5B) and cross-architecture (Qwen2.5-Math-7B) experiments provide initial generality evidence.  Our findings concern fine-grained structural pruning; whether the pattern extends to unstructured pruning~\citep{selfhealing2025} or online rollout pruning during RLVR~\citep{xu2026arrol} remains open.
Code, pruning masks, and model checkpoints will be released upon acceptance.
